V(VF, IO_A,
  "A 58-year-old man collapses in a gym. He is unresponsive, not breathing and has no pulse. The monitor shows chaotic, irregular waves of varying size with no identifiable QRS complexes. Which rhythm is present?",
  [["Ventricular fibrillation",
    "Correct. Ventricular fibrillation has no pulse and no perfusion, a rate of 0, no rhythm, no P waves and no PR interval, only uncoordinated activity in place of QRS complexes. Chaotic waves of varying size in an unresponsive, pulseless man fit exactly, and he needs defibrillation."],
   ["Polymorphic ventricular tachycardia",
    "Polymorphic ventricular tachycardia still has QRS complexes whose shape varies, as in torsades de pointes, where they twist around the baseline. This monitor shows no identifiable QRS complexes, only chaotic waves. Tell: varying QRS complexes mean polymorphic tachycardia; no QRS at all means fibrillation.", "competing diagnosis"],
   ["Asystole",
    "Asystole is a flat line with no rate, rhythm or QRS complexes. Chaotic, irregular waves of varying size are ventricular fibrillation. Tell: a flat line is asystole; chaotic waves are fibrillation.", "competing diagnosis"],
   ["Pulseless electrical activity",
    "Pulseless electrical activity shows an organized rhythm, often one that would be expected to produce a pulse, yet no pulse is felt. This monitor shows chaotic waves without any identifiable QRS. Tell: organized without a pulse is pulseless electrical activity; chaos is fibrillation.", "competing diagnosis"]],
  C(48), "test finding", "diagnosis"),

