V(ASY, IO_A,
  "A 34-year-old man is brought in after a motorcycle crash with a large thigh wound and heavy blood loss. He has no pulse. The monitor shows a regular narrow-complex rhythm at 110 per minute. Which is the most likely diagnosis?",
  [["Pulseless electrical activity",
    "Correct. A regular narrow-complex rhythm at 110, one you would expect to produce a pulse, with no pulse is pulseless electrical activity. His heavy blood loss fits hypovolemia, one of its two leading causes in adults along with hypoxia, and the rhythm is unshockable, treated with compressions and epinephrine."],
   ["Ventricular fibrillation",
    "Ventricular fibrillation is chaotic, uncoordinated activity with no organized complexes. A regular narrow-complex rhythm at 110 without a pulse is pulseless electrical activity. Tell: an organized rhythm rules out fibrillation.", "competing diagnosis"],
   ["Asystole",
    "Asystole is a flat line with no rate, rhythm or QRS. This monitor shows a regular rhythm at 110, so it is pulseless electrical activity. Tell: if there are complexes but no pulse, it is not asystole.", "competing diagnosis"],
   ["Sinus tachycardia",
    "Sinus tachycardia is a perfusing rhythm with a pulse. The same organized rhythm with no pulse is pulseless electrical activity, an arrest rhythm. Tell: the monitor alone cannot tell you; the missing pulse decides it.", "ruled out by a stated finding"]],
  C(52), "test finding", "diagnosis"),

